{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/22575-join-battle-alternate-systems","id":22575,"title":"Join Battle - Alternate Systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-03T14:02:54-08:00","id":22575,"title":"Join Battle - Alternate Systems","content":"Looking ahead, we noticed that, eventually (certainly at high Demigod and above), Join Battle will break down into &quot;I have the highest Epic Wits, so I go on 0; everyone else goes on 6 (before Opening Gambit, of course)&quot;. In our group, before counting villians, cops, or innocent bystanders, it will probably be 2 people competing over 0, and the other 5 eternally on 6 (before Opening Gambit). An alternate system proposed is that the highest Join Battle roll goes on 0; the next highest goes on 1, etc. With sufficient numbers of people involved in the same combat, you either still get a clump going on 6, or have to break them down into different slots like epic health levels (a single 0, two on 1, two on 2, etc).<br /> <br /> Another proposed solution was to have Epic Wits add its rating in dice rather than automatic successes.<br /> <br /> The theoretical benefit of the proposed new systems is that the Join Battle roll will still mean something, combat results will be more varied, and there will be less potential for infighting of the type, &quot;I always go last because of you&quot;.<br /> <br /> The possible downside of the proposed system is... that it might make the speedsters feel less special / less epic? That it makes taking Epic Wits less valuable (makes taking lots of epic wits less valuable, and taking some epic wits more valuable?)?<br /> <br /> Are there any other consequences of these potential new systems (good or bad) that we haven't accounted for?<br /> <br /> And, to ask the more general question, how have other groups felt about the huge gaps in Join Battle rolls at Demigod and above? Huge gaps in epic physical stats can be dealt with by having multiple &quot;tiers&quot; of opponents, but there is no good way to tier the initiative system built into Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:14:09-08:00","id":22583,"title":"","content":"Just have the winner of Join Battle go on Tick 0, then the second place person on Tick 1, third placers on Tick 2, and so forth. Things'll settle out as Speed comes into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:24:11-08:00","id":22588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/22575-join-battle-alternate-systems?p=22583#post22583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just have the winner of Join Battle go on Tick 0, then the second place person on Tick 1, third placers on Tick 2, and so forth. Things'll settle out as Speed comes into play.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Pretty much this.</b> There are definitely some consequences to this rule, such as reducing the value of investing heavily in epic wits, but that is entirely subjective based on how often you let your players roll Wits for non-join battle activities. I've seen some storytellers who completely neglect Wits rolls and they barely get used beyond join battle and knack/boon activation. But I recommend what Telgar suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T20:30:39-08:00","id":22859,"title":"","content":"Good to know. Thanks Telgar and Iry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","name":"sprunka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}